@id=teach-agents-the-way-of-working @maturity=specified
Feature: Teach agents the way of working

  An agent in a repository specified with sdp asks the graph before it greps, writes the rule and its
  example before the code, and never edits what sdp derives. One skill teaches that, and what only
  writing a spec needs is read when a spec is written.

  Not a skill per job: several skills that overlap are slower to learn than one.

  Rule: One skill teaches the whole way of working: orient, change the rule and its example, write the steps, implement, check and run, plan

  Rule: What only writing a spec needs — the sharp edges of the format, replacing what is live — is a reference the skill names, read on demand

  @type=quality
  Rule: The skill an agent loads first fits in 10,000 characters
